# Conway's Game of Life on the unbounded Sparse plane: every live cell adds
# 1 to each neighbour and 9 to itself, so Count By scores the whole
# neighbourhood in one pass and the next generation is the cells scoring
# 3 (birth), 11 or 12 (survival).
Cursed Energy: stdin
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Cursed Technique: Match Pattern
    Using: "{int},{int}"
    Mode: Each
Channeled Energy: Convert To Sparse Grid
    Default: 0
    Mark: 1
Simple Domain: Repeat 8
    Cursed Technique: Find Cells
        Using: (v) -> v = 1
    Cursed Technique: Map Each
        Using: (p) -> list(padd(p, point(-1, -1)), padd(p, point(-1, 0)), padd(p, point(-1, 1)), padd(p, point(0, -1)), padd(p, point(0, 1)), padd(p, point(1, -1)), padd(p, point(1, 0)), padd(p, point(1, 1)), p, p, p, p, p, p, p, p, p)
    Cursed Technique: Flatten
    Maximum Technique: Count By
        Using: (q) -> q
    Channeled Energy: Convert To Sparse Grid
        Default: 0
    Cursed Technique: Find Cells
        Using: (score) -> score = 3 or score = 11 or score = 12
    Channeled Energy: Convert To Sparse Grid
        Default: 0
        Mark: 1
Cursed Technique: Find Cells
    Using: (v) -> v = 1
Maximum Technique: Count
Reveal: stdout
